msgstr "RFC 822 长头部字段：:rfc:`822#section-3.1.1`"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:5
msgid "Dependency Groups"
msgstr "依赖群"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:7
msgid ""
"This specification defines dependency groups, a mechanism for storing "
"package requirements in ``pyproject.toml`` files such that they are not "
"included in project metadata when it is built."
msgstr ""
"本规范定义了依赖群：一种将软件包需求存储在 ``pyproject.toml`` 文件中的机制，"
"使这些需求在项目构建时不会被包含进项目元数据。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:11
msgid ""
"Dependency groups are suitable for internal development use-cases like "
"linting and testing, as well as for projects which are not built for "
"distribution, like collections of related scripts."
msgstr ""
"依赖群适用于诸如代码检查（linting）和测试之类的内部开发用途，也适用于不会构建"
"为分发包的项目，比如相关脚本的集合。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:15
msgid ""
"Fundamentally, dependency groups should be thought of as being a "
"standardized subset of the capabilities of ``requirements.txt`` files (which "
"are ``pip``-specific)."
msgstr ""
"从根本上说，应当把依赖群视为 ``requirements.txt`` 文件（这些文件是 ``pip`` 专"
"有的）能力的一个标准化子集。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:25
msgid "This is a simple table which shows ``docs`` and ``test`` groups::"
msgstr "这是一个展示 ``docs`` 和 ``test`` 群组的简单表格::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:31
msgid ""
"and a similar table which defines ``docs``, ``test``, and ``coverage`` "
"groups::"
msgstr "而下面这个类似的表格则定义了 ``docs``、``test`` 和 ``coverage`` 群组::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:39
msgid "The ``[dependency-groups]`` Table"
msgstr "``[dependency-groups]`` 表格"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:41
msgid ""
"Dependency groups are defined as a table in ``pyproject.toml`` named "
"``dependency-groups``. The ``dependency-groups`` table contains an arbitrary "
"number of user-defined keys, each of which has, as its value, a list of "
"requirements."
msgstr ""
"依赖群被定义为 ``pyproject.toml`` 中一个名为 ``dependency-groups`` 的表格"
"。``dependency-groups`` 表格包含任意数量的用户自定义键，每个键的值都是一个需"
"求列表。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:46
msgid ""
"``[dependency-groups]`` keys, sometimes also called \"group names\", must "
"be :ref:`valid non-normalized names <name-format>`. Tools which handle "
"Dependency Groups MUST :ref:`normalize <name-normalization>` these names "
"before comparisons."
msgstr ""
"``[dependency-groups]`` 的键（有时也称为“群组名”）必须是 :ref:`有效的未规范化"
"名称 <name-format>`。处理依赖群的工具必须在比较之前 :ref:`规范化 <name-"
"normalization>` 这些名称。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:51
msgid ""
"Tools SHOULD prefer to present the original, non-normalized name to users, "
"and if duplicate names are detected after normalization, tools SHOULD emit "
"an error."
msgstr ""
"工具应该优先向用户展示原始的、未规范化的名称；如果在规范化之后检测到重复的名"
"称，则工具应该报错。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:55
msgid ""
"Requirement lists, the values in ``[dependency-groups]``, may contain "
"strings, tables (``dict`` in Python), or a mix of strings and tables. "
"Strings must be valid :ref:`dependency specifiers <dependency-specifiers>`, "
"and tables must be valid Dependency Group Includes."
msgstr ""
"需求列表（即 ``[dependency-groups]`` 中的值）可以包含字符串、表格（Python 中"
"的 ``dict``）或者字符串与表格的混合。字符串必须是有效的 :ref:`依赖说明符 "
"<dependency-specifiers>`，表格必须是有效的依赖群包括。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:61
msgid "Dependency Group Include"
msgstr "依赖群包括"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:63
msgid ""
"A Dependency Group Include includes another Dependency Group in the current "
"group."
msgstr "依赖群包括（Dependency Group Include）会把另一个依赖群包含到当前群组中。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:66
msgid ""
"An include is a table with exactly one key, ``\"include-group\"``, whose "
"value is a string, the name of another Dependency Group."
msgstr ""
"包括项是一个表格，它恰好只有一个键 ``\"include-group\"``，其值为一个字符串，"
"即另一个依赖群的名称。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:69
msgid ""
"Includes are defined to be exactly equivalent to the contents of the named "
"Dependency Group, inserted into the current group at the location of the "
"include. For example, if ``foo = [\"a\", \"b\"]`` is one group, and ``bar = "
"[\"c\", {include-group = \"foo\"}, \"d\"]`` is another, then ``bar`` should "
"evaluate to ``[\"c\", \"a\", \"b\", \"d\"]`` when Dependency Group Includes "
"are expanded."
msgstr ""
"包括项的定义是：它与所指名的依赖群的内容完全等价，这些内容会被插入到当前群组"
"中该包括项所在的位置。例如，如果 ``foo = [\"a\", \"b\"]`` 是一个群组，而 "
"``bar = [\"c\", {include-group = \"foo\"}, \"d\"]`` 是另一个群组，那么当依赖"
"群包括被展开时， ``bar`` 的求值结果应该是 ``[\"c\", \"a\", \"b\", \"d\"]``。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:75
msgid ""
"Dependency Group Includes may specify the same package multiple times. Tools "
"SHOULD NOT deduplicate or otherwise alter the list contents produced by the "
"include. For example, given the following table:"
msgstr ""
"依赖群包括可以多次指定同一个软件包。工具不应对包括项产生的列表内容进行去重或"
"做出其他改动。例如，给定以下表格："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:92
msgid ""
"The resolved value of ``all`` SHOULD be ``[\"foo\", \"foo\", \"foo>1.0\", "
"\"foo<1.0\"]``. Tools should handle such a list exactly as they would handle "
"any other case in which they are asked to process the same requirement "
"multiple times with different version constraints."
msgstr ""
"``all`` 解析后的值应该是 ``[\"foo\", \"foo\", \"foo>1.0\", \"foo<1.0\"]``。工"
"具应该像处理其他任何“以不同版本约束多次处理同一需求”的情形那样来处理这样的列"
"表。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:97
msgid ""
"Dependency Group Includes may include groups containing Dependency Group "
"Includes, in which case those includes should be expanded as well. "
"Dependency Group Includes MUST NOT include cycles, and tools SHOULD report "
"an error if they detect a cycle."
msgstr ""
"依赖群包括可以包含自身又含有依赖群包括的群组，此时这些包括项也应该被展开。依"
"赖群包括不得包含循环，工具如果检测到循环，应该报错。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:102
msgid "Package Building"
msgstr "软件包构建"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:104
msgid ""
"Build backends MUST NOT include Dependency Group data in built distributions "
"as package metadata. This means that sdist ``PKG-INFO`` and wheel "
"``METADATA`` files should not include referenceable fields containing "
"dependency groups."
msgstr ""
"构建后端不得将依赖群数据作为软件包元数据包含到构建出的分发包中。这意味着 "
"sdist 的 ``PKG-INFO`` 文件和 wheel 的 ``METADATA`` 文件不应该包含带有依赖群的"
"可引用字段。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:108
msgid ""
"It is, however, valid to use dependency groups in the evaluation of dynamic "
"metadata, and ``pyproject.toml`` files included in sdists will still contain "
"``[dependency-groups]``. However, the table's contents are not part of a "
"built package's interfaces."
msgstr ""
"不过，在动态元数据的求值过程中使用依赖群是有效的，并且 sdist 中所含的 "
"``pyproject.toml`` 文件仍将包含 ``[dependency-groups]``。但是，该表格的内容并"
"不属于已构建软件包的接口。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:114
msgid "Installing Dependency Groups & Extras"
msgstr "安装依赖群 & 附加内容"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:116
msgid ""
"There is no syntax or specification-defined interface for installing or "
"referring to dependency groups. Tools are expected to provide dedicated "
"interfaces for this purpose."
msgstr ""
"目前既没有用于安装或引用依赖群的语法，也没有由本规范定义的接口。工具应当为此"
"提供专门的接口。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:120
msgid ""
"Tools MAY choose to provide the same or similar interfaces for interacting "
"with dependency groups as they do for managing extras. Tools authors are "
"advised that the specification does not forbid having an extra whose name "
"matches a Dependency Group. Separately, users are advised to avoid creating "
"dependency groups whose names match extras, and tools MAY treat such "
"matching as an error."
msgstr ""
"工具可以选择为依赖群提供交互接口，使其与管理附加功能（extras）的接口相同或类"
"似。建议工具作者注意，本规范并不禁止让附加功能与某个依赖群同名。另外，建议用"
"户避免创建与附加功能同名的依赖群，并且工具可以将这种匹配视为错误。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:128
msgid "Validation and Compatibility"
msgstr "验证与兼容性"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:130
msgid ""
"Tools supporting dependency groups may want to validate data before using "
"it. When implementing such validation, authors should be aware of the "
"possibility of future extensions to the specification, so that they do not "
"unnecessarily emit errors or warnings."
msgstr ""
"支持依赖群的工具可能希望在使用数据之前先对其进行验证。在实现此类验证时，工具"
"作者应该意识到本规范存在未来扩展的可能性，以免不必要地发出错误或警告。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:135
msgid ""
"Tools SHOULD error when evaluating or processing unrecognized data in "
"dependency groups."
msgstr "在求值或处理依赖群中无法识别的数据时，工具应该报错。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:138
msgid ""
"Tools SHOULD NOT eagerly validate the contents of *all* dependency groups "
"unless they have a need to do so."
msgstr "除非确有必要，工具不应预先验证 *所有* 依赖群的内容。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:141
msgid ""
"This means that in the presence of the following data, most tools should "
"allow the ``foo`` group to be used and only error if the ``bar`` group is "
"used:"
msgstr ""
"这意味着，在存在以下数据的情况下，大多数工具应该允许使用 ``foo`` 群组，并且只"
"在使用 ``bar`` 群组时报错："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:152
msgid ""
"There are several known cases of tools which have good cause to be stricter. "
"Linters and validators are an example, as their purpose is to validate the "
"contents of all dependency groups."
msgstr ""
"已知有若干类工具有充分的理由采取更严格的做法。代码检查工具（linter）和验证器"
"便是一例，因为它们的用途就是验证所有依赖群的内容。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:157
#: ../source/specifications/inline-script-metadata.rst:134
msgid "Reference Implementation"
msgstr "参考实现"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:159
msgid ""
"The following Reference Implementation prints the contents of a Dependency "
"Group to stdout, newline delimited. The output is therefore valid "
"``requirements.txt`` data."
msgstr ""
"下面的参考实现会把一个依赖群的内容打印到 stdout，并以换行符分隔。因此，该输出"
"是有效的 ``requirements.txt`` 数据。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-groups.rst:252
msgid "October 2024: This specification was approved through :pep:`735`."
msgstr "2024 年 10 月：本规范通过 :pep:`735` 获得批准。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:7
msgid "Dependency specifiers"
msgstr "依赖说明符"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:9
msgid ""
"This document defines the format used to specify dependencies on other "
"projects. The language defined is a compact line based format which was "
"adapted from the format originally used in ``pip`` requirements files."
msgstr ""
"本文档定义了用于指定对其他项目的依赖关系的格式。所定义的语言是一种紧凑的、基"
"于行的格式，改编自最初用于 ``pip`` 需求文件的格式。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:13
msgid ""
"The job of a dependency is to enable tools like pip [#pip]_ to find the "
"right package to install. Sometimes this is very loose - just specifying a "
"name, and sometimes very specific - referring to a specific file to install. "
"Sometimes dependencies are only relevant on one platform, or only some "
"versions are acceptable, so the language permits describing all these cases."
msgstr ""
"依赖项的作用是让 pip [#pip]_ 之类的工具能够找到合适的软件包来安装。有时这非常"
"宽松，只是指定一个名称；有时又非常具体，指向要安装的特定文件。有时依赖项只在"
"某个平台上才有意义，或者只有部分版本可以接受，因此该语言允许描述所有这些情况"
"。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:19
msgid ""
"Whether tools should be strict or permissive in their processing of "
"dependency specifiers is largely dependent on the role of the tool in the "
"wider ecosystem:"
msgstr ""
"工具在处理依赖说明符时应该严格还是宽松，很大程度上取决于该工具在整个生态系统"
"中所扮演的角色："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:22
msgid ""
"publishing tools and index servers SHOULD be strict in their processing for "
"new releases, encouraging the consistency of published specifiers to improve "
"over time"
msgstr ""
"发布工具和索引服务器在处理新发布时应该保持严格，以促使已发布说明符的一致性随"
"时间推移不断改进"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:25
msgid ""
"locking and installation tools MAY be permissive in their processing, "
"allowing consumption of older packages which may contain dependency "
"specifiers that are arguably nonsensical"
msgstr ""
"锁定工具和安装工具在处理时可以保持宽松，从而允许使用较旧的软件包，即使这些软"
"件包可能包含可以说毫无道理的依赖说明符。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:35
msgid "All features of the language shown with a name based lookup::"
msgstr "以基于名称的查找展示该语言的所有特性::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:39
msgid "A minimal URL based lookup::"
msgstr "一个最简的基于 URL 的查找::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:44
msgid "Concepts"
msgstr "概念"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:46
msgid ""
"A dependency specification always specifies a distribution name. It may "
"include extras, which expand the dependencies of the named distribution to "
"enable optional features. The version installed can be controlled using "
"version limits, or giving the URL to a specific artifact to install. Finally "
"the dependency can be made conditional using environment markers."
msgstr ""
"依赖说明符总是会指定一个分发包名称。它可以包含附加功能（extras），用于扩展所"
"指名分发包的依赖项，以启用可选特性。安装的版本可以通过版本限制来控制，也可以"
"给出要安装的特定制品的 URL。最后，还可以使用环境标记让依赖项变为有条件的。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:53
msgid "Grammar"
msgstr "语法"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:55
msgid ""
"We first cover the grammar briefly and then drill into the semantics of each "
"section later."
msgstr "我们先简要介绍语法，稍后再深入探讨各部分的语义。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:58
msgid ""
"A distribution specification is written in ASCII text. We use a parsley "
"[#parsley]_ grammar to provide a precise grammar. It is expected that the "
"specification will be embedded into a larger system which offers framing "
"such as comments, multiple line support via continuations, or other such "
"features."
msgstr ""
"分发说明符以 ASCII 文本书写。我们使用 parsley [#parsley]_ 语法来给出精确的语"
"法定义。预计该说明符会被嵌入到更大的系统中，由后者提供注释、通过续行支持多行"
"之类的框架性功能。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:63
msgid ""
"The full grammar including annotations to build a useful parse tree is "
"included at the end of this document."
msgstr "包含注解、可用于构建实用解析树的完整语法收录在本文档末尾。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:66
msgid ""
"Versions may be specified according to the rules of the :ref:`Version "
"specifier specification <version-specifiers>`. (Note: URI is defined "
"in :rfc:`std-66 <3986>`)::"
msgstr ""
"版本可以根据 :ref:`版本说明符规范 <version-specifiers>` 的规则来指定。（注意"
"：URI 的定义见 :rfc:`std-66 <3986>`）::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:77
msgid ""
"Environment markers allow making a specification only take effect in some "
"environments::"
msgstr "环境标记允许让说明符仅在部分环境中生效::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:106
msgid ""
"Optional components of a distribution may be specified using the extras "
"field::"
msgstr "分发包的可选组件可以使用 extras 字段来指定::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:115
msgid "Giving us a rule for name based requirements::"
msgstr "这就为基于名称的需求给出了一条规则::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:119
msgid "And a rule for direct reference specifications::"
msgstr "以及针对直接引用说明符的规则::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:123
msgid "Leading to the unified rule that can specify a dependency.::"
msgstr "最终得到可以指定依赖项的统一规则。::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:128
msgid "Whitespace"
msgstr "空白字符"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:130
msgid ""
"Non line-breaking whitespace is mostly optional with no semantic meaning. "
"The sole exceptions are detecting the end of a URL requirement and inside "
"user supplied constants in environment markers."
msgstr ""
"非换行空白字符大多是可选的，且不具语义。唯一的例外是检测 URL 需求的结束位置，"
"以及环境标记中用户提供的常量内部。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:137
msgid "Names"
msgstr "名称"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:139
msgid ""
"Distribution names are defined in the :ref:`Core metadata <core-metadata-"
"name>`. Names act as the primary identifier for distributions. They are "
"present in all dependency specifications, and are sufficient to be a "
"specification on their own."
msgstr ""
"分发包名称在 :ref:`核心元数据 <core-metadata-name>` 中定义。名称是分发包的主"
"要标识符。它们存在于所有依赖说明符中，并且仅凭其自身就足以构成一个说明符。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:144
msgid ""
"Valid distribution names are defined in the :ref:`name format specification "
"<name-format>`."
msgstr "有效的分发包名称在 :ref:`名称格式规范 <name-format>` 中定义。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:151
msgid "Extras"
msgstr "附加功能（extras）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:153
msgid ""
"An extra is an optional part of a distribution. Distributions can specify as "
"many extras as they wish, and each extra results in the declaration of "
"additional dependencies of the distribution **when** the extra is used in a "
"dependency specification. For instance::"
msgstr ""
"附加功能（extra）是分发包的可选部分。分发包可以按需指定任意多个附加功能，**当"
"某个附加功能被用于依赖说明符中时**，它就会导致声明该分发包的额外依赖项。例"
"如::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:160
msgid ""
"Extras union in the dependencies they define with the dependencies of the "
"distribution they are attached to. The example above would result in "
"requests being installed, and requests own dependencies, and also any "
"dependencies that are listed in the \"security\" extra of requests."
msgstr ""
"附加功能会把它们定义的依赖项与所属分发包的依赖项合并在一起。上面的例子会安装 "
"requests，以及 requests 自身的依赖项，还有 requests 的 \"security\" 附加功能"
"中列出的所有依赖项。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:165
msgid ""
"If multiple extras are listed, all the dependencies are unioned together."
msgstr "如果列出了多个附加功能，所有这些依赖项都会被合并在一起。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:167
msgid ""
"Restrictions on names for extras are defined in the :ref:`Core metadata "
"specification <core-metadata-provides-extra>`. Publication tools SHOULD "
"enforce these restrictions in dependency specifiers, while locking and "
"installation tools MAY normalize invalid extra names in order to accept "
"published metadata using core metadata versions prior to 2.3."
msgstr ""
"附加功能名称的限制在 :ref:`核心元数据规范 <core-metadata-provides-extra>` 中"
"定义。发布工具应该在依赖说明符中强制执行这些限制，而锁定工具和安装工具可以规"
"范化无效的附加功能名称，以便接受使用 2.3 之前核心元数据版本的已发布元数据。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:176
msgid "Versions"
msgstr "版本"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:178
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`Version specifier specification <version-specifiers>` for more "
"detail on both version numbers and version comparisons. Version "
"specifications limit the versions of a distribution that can be used. They "
"only apply to distributions looked up by name, rather than via a URL. "
"Version comparisons are also used in environment markers. The optional "
"brackets around a version are present for compatibility with :pep:`345` but "
"should not be generated, only accepted."
msgstr ""
"关于版本号和版本比较的更多细节，请参见 :ref:`版本说明符规范 <version-"
"specifiers>`。版本说明符会限制一个分发包可使用的版本。它们只适用于按名称查找"
"的分发包，而不适用于通过 URL 查找的分发包。版本比较同样会用于环境标记。版本两"
"侧的可选括号是为了与 :pep:`345` 兼容而保留的，但不应被生成，只需被接受。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:189
msgid "Environment Markers"
msgstr "环境标记"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:191
msgid ""
"Environment markers allow a dependency specification to provide a rule that "
"describes when the dependency should be used. For instance, consider a "
"package that needs ``pywin32`` when running on Windows. This can be "
"expressed as::"
msgstr ""
"环境标记允许依赖说明符提供一条描述该依赖项何时应被使用的规则。例如，假设有一"
"个软件包在 Windows 上运行时需要 ``pywin32``。这可以表达为::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:197
msgid ""
"A marker expression evaluates to either True or False for a given deployment "
"environment. When it evaluates to False, the dependency should be ignored."
msgstr ""
"对于给定的部署环境，标记表达式的求值结果为 True 或 False。当求值结果为 False "
"时，该依赖项应被忽略。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:200
msgid ""
"The marker language is inspired by Python itself, chosen for the ability to "
"safely evaluate it without running arbitrary code that could become a "
"security vulnerability."
msgstr ""
"标记语言借鉴了 Python 本身，这样既能安全地对其求值，又不必运行可能构成安全漏"
"洞的任意代码。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:204
msgid ""
"Markers were first defined in :pep:`345`, formally specified in :pep:`508`, "
"then subsequently amended over time (amendments since :pep:`508` are "
"recorded :ref:`at the end of this specification <dependency-specifier-"
"history>`)."
msgstr ""
"标记最初在 :pep:`345` 中定义，后在 :pep:`508` 中正式规范化，此后又随时间推移"
"陆续修订（:pep:`508` 之后的修订记录在 :ref:`本规范末尾 <dependency-specifier-"
"history>`）。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:209
msgid "Marker field types"
msgstr "标记字段类型"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:211
msgid ""
"Environment marker fields are each defined as one of the following types:"
msgstr "各个环境标记字段分别定义为以下类型之一："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:213
msgid ""
"``String``: the contents of the field are always treated as an opaque string."
msgstr "``String``：字段内容始终会被视为不透明的字符串。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:214
msgid ""
"``Set of strings``: the contents of the field are always treated as a set "
"containing opaque strings. In comparisons, the user supplied constant MUST "
"still be a single string (as set literals are not part of the marker syntax)."
msgstr ""
"``Set of strings``：字段内容始终会被视为一个包含不透明字符串的集合。在比较中"
"，用户提供的常量仍必须是单个字符串（因为集合字面量并不是标记语法的一部分）。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:217
msgid ""
"``Version``: the contents of the field are always expected to be a "
"valid :ref:`version specifier <version-specifiers>`. Publishing tools SHOULD "
"emit an error if that is not the case, but installation tools MAY fall back "
"to treating the field as a string field."
msgstr ""
"``Version``：字段内容应始终是有效的 :ref:`版本说明符 <version-specifiers>`。"
"如果不是，发布工具应该报错，但安装工具可以退而将该字段当作字符串字段处理。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:221
msgid ""
"``Version | String``: the contents of the field are expected to be a "
"valid :ref:`version specifier <version-specifiers>` on some platforms, but "
"an opaque string on others. The specifics of this distinction are field "
"dependent and whether or not tools actually make the distinction will be "
"tool dependent."
msgstr ""
"``Version | String``：字段内容在某些平台上应为有效的 :ref:`版本说明符 "
"<version-specifiers>`，而在其他平台上则是不透明的字符串。这种区分的具体细节取"
"决于具体字段，而工具是否真的做出这种区分则取决于具体工具。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:227
msgid "Marker comparisons"
msgstr "标记比较"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:229
msgid ""
"All marker comparison expressions are expected to compare a named marker "
"field against a given user supplied constant. The type of the comparison is "
"determined by the comparison operator used and the type of the named field "
"as given in :ref:`the table below <environment-marker-fields>`. Tools MAY "
"emit an error if no marker field is referenced in a comparison (that is, "
"both operands are given as constants)."
msgstr ""
"所有标记比较表达式都应将某个具名标记字段与用户提供的常量进行比较。比较的类型"
"由所用的比较运算符以及 :ref:`下表 <environment-marker-fields>` 中给出的具名字"
"段类型决定。如果比较中没有引用任何标记字段（即两个操作数都以常量形式给出），"
"工具可以报错。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:236
msgid ""
"The follow comparison operations are defined in the marker expression "
"grammar:"
msgstr "标记表达式文法中定义了以下比较运算："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:238
msgid "``==`` (for example, ``sys_platform == \"win32\"``)"
msgstr "``==`` （例如 ``sys_platform == \"win32\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:239
msgid "``!=`` (for example, ``sys_platform != \"win32\"``)"
msgstr "``!=`` （例如 ``sys_platform != \"win32\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:240
msgid "``>`` (for example, ``python_version > \"3.10\"``)"
msgstr "``>`` （例如 ``python_version > \"3.10\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:241
msgid "``>=`` (for example, ``python_version >= \"3.10\"``)"
msgstr "``>=`` （例如 ``python_version >= \"3.10\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:242
msgid "``<`` (for example, ``python_version < \"3.10\"``)"
msgstr "``<`` （例如 ``python_version < \"3.10\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:243
msgid "``<=`` (for example, ``python_version <= \"3.10\"``)"
msgstr "``<=`` （例如 ``python_version <= \"3.10\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:244
msgid "``~=`` (for example, ``python_version ~= \"3\"``)"
msgstr "``~=`` （例如 ``python_version ~= \"3\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:245
msgid ""
"``===`` (for example, ``implementation_version === \"not.a.valid.version\"``)"
msgstr "``===`` （例如 ``implementation_version === \"not.a.valid.version\"``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:246
msgid ""
"``in`` (for example, ``\"gui\" in extras``, ``\"SMP\" in platform_version``)"
msgstr "``in`` （例如 ``\"gui\" in extras``、``\"SMP\" in platform_version``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:247
msgid "``not in`` (for example, ``\"dev\" not in dependency_groups``)"
msgstr "``not in`` （例如 ``\"dev\" not in dependency_groups``）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:249
msgid ""
"For ``String`` fields, ``==``, ``!=``, ``in``, and ``not in`` are defined as "
"they are for Python strings (case sensitive, with no value normalization of "
"any kind). The use of ``~=`` or ``===`` with string fields is explicitly "
"discouraged and publishing tools SHOULD emit an error, index servers MAY "
"disallow uploads containing such environment markers, while locking and "
"installation tools MAY instead interpret them as equivalent to ``==``. The "
"use of ordered comparisons (``<``, ``<=``, ``>``, ``>=``) with string fields "
"is explicitly discouraged (as it makes no semantic sense in the packaging "
"context) and publishing tools SHOULD emit an error, index servers MAY "
"disallow uploads containing such environment markers, while locking and "
"installation tools SHOULD implement the following behavior:"
msgstr ""
"对于 ``String`` 字段，``==``、``!=``、``in`` 和 ``not in`` 的定义与 Python 字"
"符串中的相应操作一致（区分大小写，且不进行任何形式的值规范化）。明确不建议在"
"字符串字段中使用 ``~=`` 或 ``===``：发布工具应该报错，索引服务器可以拒绝包含"
"此类环境标记的上传，而锁定工具和安装工具则可以将其解释为等价于 ``==``。同样明"
"确不建议在字符串字段中使用有序比较（``<``、``<=``、``>``、``>=``），因为这在"
"打包语境中没有任何语义意义；此时发布工具应该报错，索引服务器可以拒绝包含此类"
"环境标记的上传，而锁定工具和安装工具应该实现以下行为："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:261
msgid "treat ``>=`` and ``<=`` as equivalent to ``==``"
msgstr "将 ``>=`` 和 ``<=`` 视为等价于 ``==``"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:262
msgid "treat ``>`` and ``<`` as always being False"
msgstr "将 ``>`` 和 ``<`` 视为始终为 False"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:264
msgid ""
"For ``Set of String`` fields, as there is no marker syntax for set literals, "
"the only valid operations are ``in`` and ``not in`` comparisons with a user "
"supplied string literal as the left operand. Publishing tools SHOULD emit an "
"error if environment markers attempt to use any other comparison operations "
"on these fields and index servers MAY disallow uploads containing such "
"environment markers, while locking and installation tools SHOULD treat such "
"operations as always being False."
msgstr ""
"对于 ``Set of String`` 字段，由于标记语法中没有集合字面量，唯一有效的操作是以"
"用户提供的字符串字面量作为左操作数的 ``in`` 和 ``not in`` 比较。如果环境标记"
"试图在这些字段上使用任何其他比较运算，发布工具应该报错，索引服务器可以拒绝包"
"含此类环境标记的上传，而锁定工具和安装工具应该将此类操作视为始终为 False。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:272
msgid ""
"For ``Version`` fields, the comparison operations are defined by "
"the :ref:`Version specifier specification <version-specifiers>` when either "
"both the marker field value and the user supplied constant can be parsed as "
"valid version specifiers or the ``===`` arbitrary equivalence comparison "
"operator is used. When an operator other than ``===`` is used, publishing "
"tools SHOULD emit an error if the user supplied constant cannot be parsed as "
"a valid version specifier, index servers MAY disallow uploads containing "
"such environment markers, while locking and installation tools MAY either "
"emit an error or else fall back to ``String`` field comparison logic if "
"either the marker field value or the user supplied constant cannot be parsed "
"as a valid version specifier. Note that ``in`` and ``not in`` containment "
"checks are NOT valid for ``Version`` fields and publishing tools SHOULD emit "
"an error, index servers MAY disallow uploads containing such environment "
"markers, while locking and installation tools MAY treat them as always being "
"False."
msgstr ""
"对于 ``Version`` 字段，当标记字段值和用户提供的常量都能被解析为有效的版本说明"
"符，或者使用 ``===`` 任意等价比较运算符时，比较运算由 :ref:`版本说明符规范 "
"<version-specifiers>` 定义。当使用 ``===`` 以外的运算符时，如果用户提供的常量"
"无法被解析为有效的版本说明符，发布工具应该报错，索引服务器可以拒绝包含此类环"
"境标记的上传，而锁定工具和安装工具在标记字段值或用户提供的常量无法被解析为有"
"效的版本说明符时，既可以报错，也可以退而采用 ``String`` 字段的比较逻辑。请注"
"意，``in`` 和 ``not in`` 成员检查对 ``Version`` 字段并非有效，发布工具应该报"
"错，索引服务器可以拒绝包含此类环境标记的上传，而锁定工具和安装工具可以将其视"
"为始终为 False。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:287
msgid ""
"For ``Version | String`` fields, comparison operations are defined as they "
"are for ``Version`` fields, while ``in`` and ``not in`` containment checks "
"are defined as they are for ``String`` fields. However, there is no "
"consistent cross-platform expectation that the parsing of the marker field "
"value or the user supplied constant as a valid version will succeed, so "
"tools SHOULD fall back to processing the field as a ``String`` field if "
"parsing either value as a version fails. Tools MAY emit a warning if the "
"field is expected to contain a valid version on a given platform but does "
"not in fact do so. Tools SHOULD NOT unconditionally treat such fields as "
"``String`` fields, as doing so may give incorrect answers for environment "
"markers that are appropriately scoped to the relevant platforms before "
"performing a version based comparison."
msgstr ""
"对于 ``Version | String`` 字段，比较运算的定义与 ``Version`` 字段相同，而 "
"``in`` 和 ``not in`` 成员检查的定义与 ``String`` 字段相同。然而，标记字段值或"
"用户提供的常量能否被解析为有效版本，在跨平台层面没有一致的预期，因此如果将任"
"一值解析为版本失败，工具应该退而将该字段当作 ``String`` 字段处理。如果某字段"
"在给定平台上本应包含有效的版本但实际上并没有，工具可以发出警告。工具不应该无"
"条件地将此类字段当作 ``String`` 字段处理，因为对于已在执行基于版本的比较之前"
"适当限定到相关平台的环境标记，这样做可能给出不正确的答案。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:301
msgid "Composing marker expressions"
msgstr "组合标记表达式"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:303
msgid ""
"More complex marker expressions may be composed using the ``and`` and ``or`` "
"logical operators. Parentheses may be used as necessary to control operand "
"precedence (with all comparison operations having a higher precedence)."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 ``and`` 和 ``or`` 逻辑运算符来组合出更复杂的标记表达式。必要时可以使"
"用括号来控制操作数优先级（所有比较运算都具有更高的优先级）。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:307
#: ../source/specifications/version-specifiers.rst:200
msgid "For example::"
msgstr "例如::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:313
msgid ""
"Python's comparison chaining (such as ``3.4 < python_version < 3.9``) is NOT "
"supported in environment markers (such expressions must instead be written "
"out as two separate comparisons joined by ``and``)."
msgstr ""
"环境标记不支持 Python 的比较链式写法（例如 ``3.4 < python_version < 3.9``），"
"此类表达式必须改写为由 ``and`` 连接的两个独立比较。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:318
msgid "User supplied constants"
msgstr "用户提供的常量"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:320
msgid ""
"User supplied constants are always given as strings within either ``'`` or "
"``\"`` quote marks. Triple-quoted multi-line strings are NOT permitted."
msgstr ""
"用户提供的常量总是以字符串形式给出，使用 ``'`` 或 ``\"`` 引号括起。不允许使用"
"三引号多行字符串。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:323
msgid ""
"Backslash escapes are not specified, although tools MAY support them. They "
"are not included in the specification because they add complexity and there "
"is currently no known need for treating user supplied constants as anything "
"other than either opaque strings or valid version specifiers."
msgstr ""
"规范并未定义反斜杠转义，但工具可以支持它们。之所以没有把它们纳入规范，是因为"
"它们会增加复杂性，而且目前尚无已知的需求需要把用户提供的常量当作不透明的字符"
"串或有效的版本说明符以外的任何东西来处理。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:328
msgid ""
"Similarly, non-ASCII character support is not specified, but tools MAY "
"accept them (usually based on the text encoding of the file or stream "
"containing the dependency specifier). This may be revisited in the future if "
"it becomes more common for the runtime variables typically referenced in "
"environment markers to contain non-ASCII text that users wish to perform "
"comparisons against."
msgstr ""
"类似地，规范并未定义对非 ASCII 字符的支持，但工具可以接受它们（通常依据包含该"
"依赖说明符的文件或流的文本编码）。如果环境标记中通常引用的运行时变量更常包含"
"用户希望与之比较的非 ASCII 文本，将来可能会重新考虑这一点。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:335
msgid "Unknown marker fields"
msgstr "未知标记字段"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:337
msgid ""
"References to unknown marker fields SHOULD render a package version "
"ineligible for installation or inclusion in a locked dependency tree rather "
"than resulting in a comparison that evaluates to True or False. This is so "
"that published package versions with unknown marker fields are either "
"ignored when resolving dependencies or emit a descriptive installation "
"failure, rather than producing an apparently successful installation that "
"then fails at runtime due to missing dependencies (if the unknown marker is "
"treated as False) or a potentially cryptic installation failure of a "
"dependency that is not valid for the current platform (if the unknown marker "
"is treated as True)."
msgstr ""
"对未知标记字段的引用应该使相应的软件包版本不符合安装条件，也不符合纳入锁定依"
"赖树的条件，而不是得到一个求值为 True 或 False 的比较结果。这样做的目的是：带"
"有未知标记字段的已发布软件包版本，要么在解析依赖项时被忽略，要么发出描述性的"
"安装失败信息，而不是产生表面上成功、随后却因缺少依赖项而在运行时失败的安装（"
"当未知标记被视为 False 时），也不是导致对当前平台无效的依赖项出现可能令人费解"
"的安装失败（当未知标记被视为 True 时）。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:347
msgid ""
"Variables whose value cannot be calculated on a given Python implementation "
"should evaluate to ``0`` for ``Version`` fields, and an empty string for all "
"other variables (including ``Version | String`` fields)."
msgstr ""
"在给定 Python 实现上无法计算取值的变量，对于 ``Version`` 字段应该求值为 "
"``0``，对于所有其他变量（包括 ``Version | String`` 字段）则应该求值为空字符串"
"。"

