msgid "Set of strings"
msgstr "字符串集合"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:432
msgid ""
"``{\"toml\"}`` (publishing tools SHOULD NOT permit use of this field and "
"index servers SHOULD NOT accept uploads containing such environment markers)"
msgstr ""
"``{\"toml\"}`` （发布工具不应该允许使用该字段，索引服务器不应该接受包含此类环"
"境标记的上传）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:435
msgid "``dependency_groups``"
msgstr "``dependency_groups``"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:436
msgid ""
"Used to indicate optional project internal dependencies in lock files. An "
"error except when defined by the context interpreting the specifier."
msgstr ""
"用于在锁定文件中指示项目内部的可选依赖项。除非由解释该说明符的上下文定义，否"
"则即为错误。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:440
msgid ""
"``{\"test\"}`` (publishing tools SHOULD NOT permit use of this field and "
"index servers SHOULD NOT accept uploads containing such environment markers)"
msgstr ""
"``{\"test\"}`` （发布工具不应该允许使用该字段，索引服务器不应该接受包含此类环"
"境标记的上传）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:444
msgid ""
"For backwards compatibility with older locking and installation tools, the "
"``extras`` and ``dependency_groups`` fields are currently only valid for use "
"in ``packages.marker`` fields in :ref:`lock files <lock-file-spec>`. For "
"these comparisons, the ``extras`` and ``dependency_groups`` sets used for "
"the marker evaluation refer to the *currently selected* extras and "
"dependency groups when installing from the lock file, not the full set of "
"defined extras and dependency groups listed in the corresponding top level "
"lock file fields. The interface for selecting which extras and dependency "
"groups to install is tool dependent. Publishing tools SHOULD emit an error "
"if projects attempt to reference the ``extras`` or ``dependency_groups`` "
"fields in their published dependency declaration metadata, and index servers "
"SHOULD NOT accept uploads referencing these fields. Outside lock file "
"processing, marker evaluation environments DO NOT need to define these "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"为了与较旧的锁定工具和安装工具保持向后兼容，``extras`` 和 "
"``dependency_groups`` 字段目前仅在 :ref:`锁定文件 <lock-file-spec>` 的 "
"``packages.marker`` 字段中有效。对于这些比较，标记求值所用的 ``extras`` 和 "
"``dependency_groups`` 集合，指的是从锁定文件安装时 *当前选定的* 附加功能（"
"extras）和依赖群，而不是锁定文件相应顶层字段中列出的全部已定义附加功能（"
"extras）和依赖群。选择安装哪些附加功能（extras）和依赖群的接口因工具而异。如"
"果项目试图在其发布的依赖声明元数据中引用 ``extras`` 或 ``dependency_groups`` "
"字段，发布工具应该报错，索引服务器不应该接受引用这些字段的上传。在锁定文件处"
"理之外，标记求值环境不需要定义这些字段。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:458
msgid ""
"The ``extra`` field is also special, as it expects set-like behaviour, but "
"predates the addition of ``Set of strings`` as a defined marker field type. "
"It only supports one operation, ``extra == \"name\"``, which is similar to "
"``\"name\" in extras``. ``extra != \"name\"`` SHOULD NOT be used anymore and "
"MAY be rejected or evaluated to false. For dependency marker evaluations, "
"the set of extra names used for these comparisons is the full set of "
"requested extras for *that particular package*, whether requested directly "
"in a top level dependency declaration, or indirectly in a transitive "
"dependency declaration. Other comparison operations on ``extra`` are not "
"defined and publishing tools SHOULD emit an error, index servers MAY "
"disallow uploads containing such environment markers, while locking and "
"installation tools SHOULD evaluate them as False."
msgstr ""
"``extra`` 字段也很特殊：它期望类似集合的行为，但其出现早于 ``Set of "
"strings`` 作为一种已定义的标记字段类型被加入的时间。它只支持一种操作，即 "
"``extra == \"name\"``，类似于 ``\"name\" in extras``。``extra != \"name\"`` "
"不应该再被使用，工具可以拒绝它，也可以将其求值为 false。对于依赖项标记求值，"
"这些比较所用的附加功能名称集合，是 *该特定软件包* 所请求的附加功能（extras）"
"的完整集合，无论这些附加功能是在顶层依赖声明中直接请求的，还是在传递依赖声明"
"中间接请求的。对 ``extra`` 的其他比较操作均未定义，发布工具应该报错，索引服务"
"器可以拒绝包含此类环境标记的上传，而锁定工具和安装工具应该将其求值为 False。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:471
msgid ""
"Unlike the newer ``extras`` field, environment markers using this field "
"SHOULD be accepted by both publishing tools and index servers. Marker "
"evaluation environments intended for project dependency declarations will "
"typically need to handle evaluation of ``extra`` field comparisons, while "
"other evaluations of environment markers will not generally need to do so. "
"The legacy ``extra`` comparison syntax is NOT permitted in lock file "
"``packages.marker`` fields, and installation tools SHOULD reject lock files "
"containing such comparisons as invalid."
msgstr ""
"与较新的 ``extras`` 字段不同，使用该字段的环境标记应该同时被发布工具和索引服"
"务器接受。面向项目依赖声明的标记求值环境通常需要处理 ``extra`` 字段比较的求值"
"，而其他环境标记求值一般不需要这样做。旧式的 ``extra`` 比较语法不得用于锁定文"
"件的 ``packages.marker`` 字段，安装工具应该将包含此类比较的锁定文件视为无效并"
"予以拒绝。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:480
msgid ""
"The ``implementation_version`` marker variable is derived "
"from :py:data:`sys.implementation.version <sys.implementation>`:"
msgstr ""
"``implementation_version`` 标记变量派生自 "
":py:data:`sys.implementation.version <sys.implementation>`："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:500
msgid "Complete Grammar"
msgstr "完整语法"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:502
msgid "The complete parsley grammar::"
msgstr "完整的 parsley 语法::"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:609
msgid "A test program - if the grammar is in a string ``grammar``:"
msgstr "一个测试程序，前提是该语法保存在字符串 ``grammar`` 中："

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:683
msgid "November 2015: This specification was approved through :pep:`508`."
msgstr "2015 年 11 月：本规范通过 :pep:`508` 获得批准。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:684
msgid ""
"July 2019: The definition of ``python_version`` was `changed <python-version-"
"change_>`_ from ``platform.python_version()[:3]`` to "
"``'.'.join(platform.python_version_tuple()[:2])``, to accommodate potential "
"future versions of Python with 2-digit major and minor versions (e.g. 3.10). "
"[#future_versions]_"
msgstr ""
"2019 年 7 月：``python_version`` 的定义已 `更改 <python-version-change_>`_，"
"从 ``platform.python_version()[:3]`` 改为 ``'.'.join"
"(platform.python_version_tuple()[:2])``，以适应将来可能出现的主版本号和次版本"
"号为两位数的 Python 版本（例如 3.10）。 [#future_versions]_"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:689
msgid ""
"March 2022: Standardised the normalization of extra names at publication "
"time (for core metadata 2.3 and later) through :pep:`685`"
msgstr ""
"2022 年 3 月：通过 :pep:`685` 标准化了发布时附加功能名称的规范化处理（适用于"
"核心元数据 2.3 及更高版本）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:691
msgid ""
"June 2024: The definition of ``version_many`` was changed to allow trailing "
"commas, matching with the behavior of the Python implementation that has "
"been in use since late 2022."
msgstr ""
"2024 年 6 月：``version_many`` 的定义已更改为允许末尾逗号，与自 2022 年末以来"
"一直沿用的 Python 实现的行为保持一致。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:694
msgid ""
"April 2025: Added ``extras`` and ``dependency_groups`` marker field "
"for :ref:`lock-file-spec` as approved through :pep:`751`."
msgstr ""
"2025 年 4 月：为 :ref:`lock-file-spec` 添加了 ``extras`` 和 "
"``dependency_groups`` 标记字段，经 :pep:`751` 批准。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:696
#: ../source/specifications/name-normalization.rst:56
msgid ""
"August 2025: The suggested name validation regex was fixed to match the "
"field specification (it previously finished with ``$`` instead of ``\\Z``, "
"incorrectly permitting trailing newlines)"
msgstr ""
"2025 年 8 月：修正了建议的名称验证正则表达式，使其与字段规范相符（此前该表达"
"式以 ``$`` 结尾而非 ``\\Z``，会错误地允许尾部换行符）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:699
msgid ""
"December 2025: Ensure ``===`` is before ``==`` in grammar, to allow "
"arbitrary equality comparisons to be parsed."
msgstr ""
"2025 年 12 月：确保文法中 ``===`` 位于 ``==`` 之前，以允许解析任意相等性比较"
"。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:701
msgid ""
"January 2026: Amend the definition of environment marker comparison "
"operations to restrict version comparison semantics to fields where they "
"make sense, make extra name restrictions more explicit, adjust the way "
"ordered comparisons are defined for strings, and make the fallback from "
"version comparisons to string comparisons when version parsing fails "
"optional. Also provide different tool behaviour recommendations for "
"publishing tools vs installation tools. This brought the nominal "
"specification into line with the way tools actually work. "
"[#marker_comparison_logic]_"
msgstr ""
"2026 年 1 月：修订了环境标记比较操作的定义，将版本比较语义限制在其有意义的字"
"段上，使 extra 名称限制更加明确，调整了字符串有序比较的定义方式，并将版本解析"
"失败时从版本比较回退到字符串比较的行为改为可选。此外，还针对发布工具与安装工"
"具分别给出了不同的工具行为建议。这使名义规范与工具的实际工作方式保持一致。 "
"[#marker_comparison_logic]_"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:709
msgid ""
"January 2026: fix outdated references to other documents that were "
"inadvertently retained from :pep:`508`"
msgstr "2026 年 1 月：修复了从 :pep:`508` 中无意遗留的指向其他文档的过时引用"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:711
msgid ""
"July 2026: Explain that ``extra != \"name\"`` is not (properly) supported "
"(https://discuss.python.org/t/ban-negative-extras-for-extras-marker/"
"108022/24)"
msgstr ""
"2026 年 7 月：说明了 ``extra != \"name\"`` 未（正式）得到支持（https://"
"discuss.python.org/t/ban-negative-extras-for-extras-marker/108022/24）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:718
msgid ""
"pip, the recommended installer for Python packages (http://"
"pip.readthedocs.org/en/stable/)"
msgstr "pip，推荐的 Python 软件包安装工具（http://pip.readthedocs.org/en/stable/）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:721
msgid "The parsley PEG library. (https://pypi.python.org/pypi/parsley/)"
msgstr "parsley PEG 库（https://pypi.python.org/pypi/parsley/）。"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:724
msgid ""
"Future Python versions might be problematic with the definition of "
"Environment Marker Variable ``python_version`` (https://github.com/python/"
"peps/issues/560)"
msgstr ""
"未来的 Python 版本可能会与环境标记变量 ``python_version`` 的定义产生问题（"
"https://github.com/python/peps/issues/560）"

#: ../source/specifications/dependency-specifiers.rst:728
msgid ""
"Resolving inconsistencies between actual tool behavior and the nominal "
"definitions of environment marker field comparisons (https://"
"discuss.python.org/t/spec-change-bugfix-dependency-specifiers-simplification-"
"pep-508/105203)"
msgstr ""
"解决工具实际行为与环境标记字段比较名义定义之间的不一致（https://"
"discuss.python.org/t/spec-change-bugfix-dependency-specifiers-simplification-"
"pep-508/105203）"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:6
msgid "Recording the Direct URL Origin of installed distributions"
msgstr "记录已安装分发包的直接 URL 来源"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:8
msgid ""
"This document specifies a :file:`direct_url.json` file in the ``*.dist-"
"info`` directory of an installed distribution, to record the Direct URL "
"Origin of the distribution. The general structure and usage of ``*.dist-"
"info`` directories is described in :ref:`recording-installed-packages`."
msgstr ""
"本文档规定了已安装分发包的 ``*.dist-info`` 目录中的一个 "
":file:`direct_url.json` 文件，用于记录该分发包的直接 URL 来源。 ``*.dist-"
"info`` 目录的一般结构和用法在 :ref:`recording-installed-packages` 中有所描述"
"。"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:17
msgid ""
"The :file:`direct_url.json` file MUST be created in the :file:`*.dist-info` "
"directory by installers when installing a distribution from a requirement "
"specifying a direct URL reference (including a VCS URL)."
msgstr ""
"当安装工具根据指定了直接 URL 引用（包括 VCS URL）的需求安装分发包时，必须在 "
":file:`*.dist-info` 目录中创建 :file:`direct_url.json` 文件。"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:21
#: ../source/specifications/recording-installed-packages.rst:222
msgid ""
"This file MUST NOT be created when installing a distribution from an other "
"type of requirement (i.e. name plus version specifier)."
msgstr "当根据其他类型的需求（即名称加版本说明符）安装分发包时，不得创建此文件。"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:24
msgid ""
"This JSON file MUST be a UTF-8 encoded, :rfc:`8259` compliant, serialization "
"of the :doc:`direct-url-data-structure`."
msgstr ""
"此 JSON 文件必须是 :doc:`direct-url-data-structure` 的序列化形式，采用 UTF-8 "
"编码并符合 :rfc:`8259`。"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:29
msgid ""
"When the requested URL has the file:// scheme and points to a local "
"directory that happens to contain a VCS checkout, installers MUST NOT "
"attempt to infer any VCS information and therefore MUST NOT output any VCS "
"related information (such as ``vcs_info``) in :file:`direct_url.json`."
msgstr ""
"当请求的 URL 使用 file:// 方案并指向恰好包含 VCS 检出（checkout）的本地目录时"
"，安装工具不得尝试推断任何 VCS 信息，因此也不得在 :file:`direct_url.json` 中"
"输出任何 VCS 相关信息（如 ``vcs_info``）。"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:36
msgid ""
"As a general rule, installers should as much as possible preserve the "
"information that was provided in the requested URL when "
"generating :file:`direct_url.json`. For example user:password environment "
"variables should be preserved and ``requested_revision`` should reflect the "
"revision that was provided in the requested URL as faithfully as possible. "
"This information is however *enriched* with more precise data, such as "
"``commit_id``."
msgstr ""
"作为一般规则，安装工具在生成 :file:`direct_url.json` 时，应尽可能保留请求的 "
"URL 中所提供的信息。例如，应保留 user:password 环境变量，并且 "
"``requested_revision`` 应尽可能忠实地反映请求的 URL 中提供的修订版本。不过，"
"这些信息会借助更精确的数据（如 ``commit_id``）得到 *增强*。"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:45
msgid "Example pip commands and their effect on direct_url.json"
msgstr "pip 命令示例及其对 direct_url.json 的影响"

#: ../source/specifications/direct-url.rst:47
msgid "Commands that generate a ``direct_url.json``:"
msgstr "会生成 ``direct_url.json`` 的命令："

